    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80bf-ab14-e8f6ccd17953",
      "type": "quote",
      "richText": [
        [
          "In Spring Boot, you connect to a relational database by setting properties like spring.datasource.url, username, and password in the application.properties file. Spring Boot auto-configures the DataSource and uses it with JPA or JDBC to interact with the database. For example, I can use Spring Data JPA with MySQL to persist entities using simple interfaces like JpaRepository, without writing SQL manually."
        ]
      ]
